### Describe the bug

Removing `javax.decorator.Decorator` in extension with AnnotationsTransformerBuildItem has no effect as `io.quarkus.arc.processor.BeanDeployment` uses only `beanArchiveImmutableIndex `and doesn't check against AnnotationStore (which actually applies annotation transformations) if decorator annotation was removed within some `AnnotationsTransformerBuildItem ` build step. 

See here:
https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/6faf038f8964c9685a2028d2fa56d3b13205e2b2/independent-projects/arc/processor/src/main/java/io/quarkus/arc/processor/BeanDeployment.java#L1287

### Expected behavior

_No response_

### Actual behavior

_No response_

### How to Reproduce?

Write quarkus extension with following deployment processor

```java
import io.quarkus.arc.deployment.AnnotationsTransformerBuildItem;
import io.quarkus.arc.processor.AnnotationsTransformer;
import io.quarkus.arc.processor.DotNames;
import io.quarkus.deployment.annotations.BuildStep;
import io.quarkus.deployment.builditem.FeatureBuildItem;

public class MyDeploymentProcessor {

    public static final String FEATURE_NAME = "mytest";

    @BuildStep
    FeatureBuildItem feature() {
        return new FeatureBuildItem(FEATURE_NAME);
    }

    @BuildStep
    public AnnotationsTransformerBuildItem removeDecorators() {
        return new AnnotationsTransformerBuildItem(new AnnotationsTransformer() {

            @Override
            public boolean appliesTo(org.jboss.jandex.AnnotationTarget.Kind kind) {
                return true;
            }

            @Override
            public void transform(TransformationContext context) {
                context.transform()
                        .remove(ann -> DotNames.DECORATOR.equals(ann.name()))
                        .done();
            }

        });
    }
}
```
And implement decorators
e.g.:

```java
 
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;

import javax.annotation.Priority;
import javax.decorator.Decorator;
import javax.decorator.Delegate;
import javax.enterprise.context.Dependent;
import javax.inject.Inject;

import org.jboss.shrinkwrap.api.ShrinkWrap;
import org.jboss.shrinkwrap.api.asset.EmptyAsset;
import org.jboss.shrinkwrap.api.spec.JavaArchive;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.extension.RegisterExtension;

import io.quarkus.test.QuarkusUnitTest;

public class DecoratorTest {

    @RegisterExtension
    static final QuarkusUnitTest unitTest = new QuarkusUnitTest()
            .setArchiveProducer(() -> ShrinkWrap.create(JavaArchive.class)
                    .addAsManifestResource(EmptyAsset.INSTANCE, "beans.xml"));

    public interface TestInterface {
        String getValue();
    }

    @Dependent
    public static class DefaultBean implements TestInterface {

        @Override
        public String getValue() {
            return "Default";
        }

    }

    @Priority(1)
    @Decorator
    public static class MyDecorator implements TestInterface {

        @Inject
        @Delegate
        TestInterface delegate;

        @Override
        public String getValue() {
            return "Decorator " + delegate.getValue();
        }

    }

    @Inject
    TestInterface bean;

    @Test
    public void decorator_is_ignored() {
        //fails with DecoratorTest.decorator_is_ignored:60 expected: <Default> but was: <Decorator Default>
        assertEquals("Default", bean.getValue());
    }

}

```


